          <div class="sc-iGgVNO cqnyEr pf-icon-left" data-scrolling="false" data-multiple="false" draggable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion">
           <div data-pf-type="Accordion.Content.Wrapper" class="sc-gsFSjX jrgsRq">
            <button type="button" class="sc-fqkwJk fCNPsG pf-anchor" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion.Header"><i class="pfa pfa-plus pfa-arrow"></i><span data-text-editing="true" class="">What’s the best way to store coffee from your store?</span></button>
            <div data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion.Content" class="sc-dcJtft hDKXay" style="display: none;">
             <div class="sc-jXbVAB kNtuek pf-r pf-r-eh" draggable="true" data-pf-type="Row" style="--s-xs: 15px; --s-lg: 0px;">
              <div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs: 12; --c-sm: 12; --c-md: 12; --c-lg: 12;">
               <div draggable="true" data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-dExXmK fNpoDq">
                <p class="sc-kAkozD iOjmJ pf-caret-color-transparent pf-word-wrap-break-word" contenteditable="true" spellcheck="false" draggable="true" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">Once roasted, coffee begins to lose its flavor the longer it’s exposed to air and moisture. We recommend that you store it in an airtight container in a cool, dark place and grind it just before brewing. Coffee in an unopened FlavorLock bag will stay fresh for several months.</p>
               </div>
              </div>
             </div>
            </div>
           </div>
